# Replication Report: Xu et al. (2019)
## "Comparative Genomic Insights into Secondary Metabolism Biosynthetic Gene Cluster Distributions of Marine *Streptomyces*"

**Paper:** Xu L, Ye KX, Dai WH, Sun C, Xu LH, Han BN. *Marine Drugs* 17(9):498 (2019).
**DOI:** [10.3390/md17090498](https://doi.org/10.3390/md17090498)
**PMC:** PMC6780079 — **PMID:** 31454987
**Open access:** ✅ (CC BY 4.0 / MDPI)

**Report Date:** 2026-06-17
**Analyst:** Ollie (OpenClaw AI) — BVBRC Replication Project (Wave 4, target #18)
**Verdict:** **SPOT-CHECK PASS** (corpus available, genome-size scaling supports the reported BGC range; antiSMASH/pan-genome rerun out of scope)

---

## 1. Paper

Analyses 87 marine *Streptomyces* genomes via pan-genomics (123,302 orthologous clusters), phylogenomics (three clades I/II/III with 23/38/22 strains), and antiSMASH-based SMBGC mining (per-genome BGC counts ranging from 16 to 84). Concludes that BGC distribution patterns correlate with both phylotype (clade) and ecotype (sediment vs marine-invertebrate source).

## 2. Claims tested

