## 8. Tools / Datasets / Hardware

**Used:** Europe PMC, BV-BRC, curl, python3.
**Required for full replication (not used):** antiSMASH v5/v6, OrthoMCL or GET_HOMOLOGUES, IQ-TREE/RAxML, MAFFT, the paper's Supplementary Table S1 (87-strain list with NCBI accessions). All open-source; ~16 CPU-cores × 1 week is a realistic budget.

## 9. Limitations

- Did not re-run antiSMASH on any genome; the 16–84 BGC range is only plausibility-checked, not verified.
- Did not parse the paper's Supplementary Table S1 strain list to confirm 1-to-1 availability of all 87 isolates in BV-BRC.
- BV-BRC's `isolation_source` field is not fully populated for all marine isolates, so marine-only filtering via keyword search is incomplete; the actual marine subset is much larger than 5 samples we returned.
- antiSMASH version differences (v4 vs v6) can shift per-genome BGC counts by ±10–20%; a rerun today would not necessarily match the paper exactly.
